id: pm-unit-wasm
title: Node 22 revert proof misses TAP UnitRefusal failures
description: "test/revert.acceptance.ts treats a safeguard removal as behavioral only when the child output matches AssertionError, a missing expected rejection, or UnitRefusal followed by a colon. Node 22's test runner prints the refusal as TAP fields name and error, so the same behavioral failure is rejected and the release gate stays red."
type: Issue
pm_format_version: 2
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags[2]: ci,tests
created_at: "2026-11-17T18:28:32.192Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-17T22:42:00.112Z"
author: pi-glm
repro_steps: "On Node 22, run npm run test:revert. The context-compatibility removal is the failing case."
expected_result: A behavioral UnitRefusal on Node 22 and Node 26 is classified as behavioral. Syntax errors and module load errors are still rejected.
actual_result: "Node 22 prints not ok for comparison refuses dimensions kinds subjects populations digests and windows, and that output does not match the colon-suffixed UnitRefusal pattern. Node 26 passes."
comments[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-17T18:28:51.282Z",pi-glm,"Reproduced on Node 22.19.0 and Node 26.13.0. Node 22 TAP splits the refusal into name and error fields, so UnitRefusal: does not occur. Node 26 spec output contains UnitRefusal: Unit dimensions differ. A load failure is ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND plus error: test failed, and a syntax failure is SyntaxError. Neither has the behavioral name field."
  "2026-11-17T22:13:28.587Z",codex-sol,"Rechecking the actual output for normalization and context mutations. The initial classifier change stopped on Node 26 normalization, so both reporters need coverage for assertions as well as refusal errors."
  "2026-11-17T22:16:36.204Z",codex-sol,"Captured both baseline mutations. Node 22 context failure prints name: UnitRefusal and code: dimension_mismatch in TAP diagnostics. Node 26 prints UnitRefusal followed by its message and inserts [ERR_ASSERTION] between AssertionError and the colon for normalization. The proof now requests TAP explicitly and reads error identity from diagnostic fields."
  "2026-11-17T22:33:26.267Z",codex-sol,The Node 26 full proof passed all 55 behavioral reverts and the restored suite in 956 seconds. The first Node 22 linked run classified all 55 successfully before its 900-second aggregate PM limit interrupted the restored suite. The repeat uses a 30-minute aggregate PM runner budget with the same per-child watchdogs.
  "2026-11-17T22:41:59.065Z",codex-sol,"The repeat passed end to end on Node 22.19.0 in 434 seconds through the linked test runner. Node 22.19.0 and Node 26.13.0 each accepted all 55 behavioral reverts and passed the restored suite. The two TAP classifier tests passed on both majors. Typecheck, lint and changelog full/check passed. Commit: Make pm-unit revert proofs reporter-independent."
files[3]{path,scope}:
